                BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION

IN THE MATTER OF THE APPLICATION OF EL PASO                         )
ELECTRIC COMPANY FOR REVISION OF ITS RETAIL                         )   Docket No. 25-00082-UT
ELECTRIC RATES PURSUANT TO ADVICE NOTICE                            )
NO. 317                                                             )

           ORDER DENYING JOINT MOTION TO REJECT EPE’S RESPONSE AND
                       GRANTING REQUEST TO FILE REPLY

            THIS MATTER comes before the Hearing Examiners upon the Joint Motion for an Order

Rejecting El Paso Electric Company’s (“EPE”) Late-Filed Response in Opposition to the Joint

Motion for Clarification and Reconsideration or, in the Alternative, for Leave to Reply to that

Response (“Motion”), filed September 28, 2026, by the City of Las Cruces, Doña Ana County,

Stephen Fischmann, Philip B. Simpson, and Dwight Eggers (collectively, “Joint Movants”). The

Motion is denied in part and granted in part, as explained further below.

            1.     The request to reject EPE’s Response in Opposition to the Joint Motion For

Clarification and Reconsideration (“Response”) is denied. The Joint Movants contend that their

September 8, 2026, Joint Motion for Clarification and Reconsideration of Order Establishing

Revised Procedural Schedule (“Motion for Clarification”) was governed by Rule 1.2.2.37(F)

NMAC and, consequently, that EPE was required to respond within five days.1 EPE treated the

filing as a motion governed by the generally applicable response provisions of Rule 1.2.2.12(C)

NMAC and filed its response accordingly.2 Under the circumstances presented here, the Hearing

Examiners find that EPE’s reliance on Rule 1.2.2.12(C) NMAC was reasonable and permitted.

            2.     Rule 1.2.2.12(C) NMAC establishes the generally applicable time for responding

to motions, while Rule 1.2.2.37(F) NMAC establishes a separate response period for a motion for



1
    Motion (September 28, 2026) at 3.
2
    Id. at 4.
                  BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Order Denying Joint Motion to Reject EPE’s Response          Docket No. 25-00082-UT



rehearing. The Joint Movants’ choice to characterize their underlying Motion for Clarification as

a motion governed by Rule 1.2.2.37(F) NMAC does not, on its own, establish that the five-day

response period provided by that Rule displaced the otherwise applicable provisions of Rule

1.2.2.12(C) NMAC. Particularly where the underlying motion sought reconsideration and

clarification of interlocutory procedural rulings rather than rehearing of a determination on the

merits, EPE’s reliance on Rule 1.2.2.12(C) NMAC was reasonable.

           3.   The Hearing Examiners need not resolve any other arguments advanced by the Joint

Movants concerning the proper characterization of requests for clarification or reconsideration of

interlocutory orders, particularly considering the fact that the Joint Movants failed to identify any

material prejudice resulting from the timing of EPE’s Response, which was filed before disposition

of the underlying Motion for Clarification and is available for consideration with the other relevant

filings.

           4.   The Joint Movants’ alternative request for leave to file the Joint Reply to EPE’s

Response (“Reply”), attached to their Motion, is granted. Because EPE’s Response will be

considered, permitting the Joint Movants’’ Reply provides a complete record of the parties’

respective positions and allows the underlying Joint Motion for Clarification to be resolved on its

merits.

           5.   No further briefing by any party concerning the timeliness or propriety of these

filings is authorized absent further order of the Hearing Examiners.




                                                 2
                  BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Order Denying Joint Motion to Reject EPE’s Response          Docket No. 25-00082-UT



        IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED:

        A.     The Joint Movants’ request to reject or strike EPE’s Response is DENIED.

        B.     The Joint Movants’ alternative request for leave to file their Reply, attached as

Exhibit A to their Motion, is GRANTED.

        C.     No further briefing concerning the timeliness, acceptance, or propriety of EPE’s

Response or the Joint Parties’ Reply shall be filed absent prior authorization from the Hearing

Examiners.

        D.     This Order does not determine the merits of the pending Joint Motion for

Clarification, which will be addressed separately.

        ISSUED under the seal of the Commission at Santa Fe, New Mexico, on September 29,
2026.


                              NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION



                              __________________________
                              Keven Gedko
